there ain't no way you're
going to take them boys

250
00:49:08.525 --> 00:49:10.151
without setting off
them bombs.

251
00:49:10.235 --> 00:49:11.986
I have no doubt.

252
00:49:12.070 --> 00:49:15.364
And. yes. some Germans will die.
Yes. it will ruin the evening.

253
00:49:15.449 --> 00:49:18.367
And. yes. Goebbels will be
very. very. very mad at you

254
00:49:18.452 --> 00:49:20.536
for what you've done
to his big night.

255
00:49:21.788 --> 00:49:24.081
But you won't get Hitler.
you won't get Goebbels.

256
00:49:24.166 --> 00:49:27.209
you won't get Goring.
and you won't get Bormann.

257
00:49:27.294 --> 00:49:29.879
And you need all four
to end the war.

258
00:49:31.548 --> 00:49:34.717
But if I don't pick up
this phone right here.

259
00:49:34.801 --> 00:49:37.136
you may very well
get all four.

260
00:49:38.388 --> 00:49:43.225
And if you get all four.
you end the war

261
00:49:44.478 --> 00:49:45.728
tonight.

262
00:49:47.105 --> 00:49:48.647
So. gentlemen.

263
00:49:49.357 --> 00:49:52.568
let's discuss the prospect
of ending the war tonight.

264
00:49:55.489 --> 00:49:57.323
So. the way I see it.

265
00:49:57.407 --> 00:50:01.619
since Hitler's death or possible
rescue rests solely on my reaction.

266
00:50:02.287 --> 00:50:03.871
if I do nothing.

267
00:50:04.289 --> 00:50:06.999
it's as if I'm causing his
death even more than yourselves.

268
00:50:07.084 --> 00:50:08.334
Wouldn't you agree?

269
00:50:09.002 --> 00:50:10.336
I guess so.

270
00:50:12.923 --> 00:50:14.924
How about you.
Utivich?

271
00:50:15.008 --> 00:50:16.634
I guess so. too.

272
00:50:22.182 --> 00:50:23.432
Gentlemen.
I have no intention

273
00:50:23.517 --> 00:50:26.602
of killing Hitler and killing Goebbels
and killing Goring and killing Bormann.

274
00:50:26.686 --> 00:50:29.438
not to mention winning the war
single-handedly for the Allies.

275
00:50:29.523 --> 00:50:33.275
only later to find myself
standing before a Jewish tribunal.

276
00:50:35.362 --> 00:50:38.906
If you want to win
the war tonight.

277
00:50:40.534 --> 00:50:42.701
we have to make a deal.

278
00:50:45.705 --> 00:50:47.456
What kind of deal?

279
00:50:47.541 --> 00:50:50.084
The kind you wouldn't
have the authority to make.

280
00:50:50.168 --> 00:50:54.713
However. I'm sure this mission
of yours has a commanding officer.

281
00:50:55.715 --> 00:50:57.049
A general.

282
00:50:57.717 --> 00:50:59.385
I'm betting for...

283
00:51:01.096 --> 00:51:03.013
OSS would be my guess.

284
00:51:06.935 --> 00:51:09.395
That's a bingo!

285
00:51:12.399 --> 00:51:14.900
Is that the way you say it?
"That's a bingo."

286
00:51:14.985 --> 00:51:16.861
You just say. "Bingo."

287
00:51:16.945 --> 00:51:19.196
Bingo! How fun.

288
00:51:21.616 --> 00:51:24.702
But I digress. Where were we?
Yeah! Make a deal.

289
00:51:25.245 --> 00:51:29.665
Over there is a very capable
two-way radio and sitting behind it

290
00:51:29.749 --> 00:51:33.919
is a more than capable
radio operator named Hermann.

291
00:51:34.254 --> 00:51:36.589
Get me someone on the
other end of that radio

292
00:51:36.673 --> 00:51:39.717
with the power of the pen
to authorize my.

293
00:51:39.801 --> 00:51:42.720
let's call it. the terms
of my conditional surrender.

294
00:51:42.804 --> 00:51:45.222
If that tastes better
going down.

295
00:51:46.016 --> 00:51:47.266
You know.
where I'm from...

296
00:51:47.350 --> 00:51:49.226
Yeah?
Where is that exactly?

297
00:51:49.311 --> 00:51:51.353
Maynardville.
Tennessee.

298
00:51:51.438 --> 00:51:53.898
I've done my share
of bootlegging.

299
00:51:54.107 --> 00:51:57.776
Up there. if you engage in what the
federal government calls illegal activity.

300
00:51:57.861 --> 00:51:59.987
but what we call just a man trying
to make a living for his family

301
00:52:00.071 --> 00:52:04.491
selling moonshine liquor. it
behooves oneself to keep his wits.

302
00:52:06.453 --> 00:52:09.872
Long story short. we hear
a story too good to be true.

303
00:52:10.540 --> 00:52:11.790
it ain't.

304
00:52:13.627 --> 00:52:16.378
Sitting in your chair.
I would probably say the same thing.

305
00:52:16.463 --> 00:52:21.175
and 999. 999 times out of a million.
you would be correct.

306
00:52:23.178 --> 00:52:26.764
But in the pages of history.
every once in a while.

307
00:52:27.349 --> 00:52:30.726
fate reaches out
and extends its hand.

308
00:52:37.567 --> 00:52:39.526
What shall
the history books read?

309
00:53:06.388 --> 00:53:09.598
I implore you.
We must destroy that tower.

310
00:53:11.017 --> 00:53:12.643
Sarge. that tower...

311
00:53:32.205 --> 00:53:34.123
The tower stands!

312
00:53:41.256 --> 00:53:43.757
Psst! Psst!

313
00:56:13.867 --> 00:56:16.034
So when the military
history of this night is written.

314
00:56:16.119 --> 00:56:19.788
it will be recorded that I
was part of Operation Kino

315
00:56:19.873 --> 00:56:22.666
from the very beginning
as a double agent.

316
00:56:22.750 --> 00:56:26.795
Anything I've done in
my guise as an SS Colonel

317
00:56:26.880 --> 00:56:29.923
was sanctioned by the OSS
as a necessary evil

318
00:56:30.008 --> 00:56:32.718
to establish my cover
with the Germans.

319
00:56:32.927 --> 00:56:36.221
And it was my placement of
Lieutenant Raine's dynamite

320
00:56:36.306 --> 00:56:39.266
in Hitler and Goebbels' opera
box that assured their demise.

321
00:56:56.409 --> 00:56:59.411
By the way. that last
part is actually true.

322
00:56:59.496 --> 00:57:04.416
I want my full military pension
and benefits under my proper rank.

323
00:57:04.751 --> 00:57:07.169
I want to receive the
Congressional Medal of Honor

324
00:57:07.253 --> 00:57:11.215
for my invaluable assistance in
the toppling of the Third Reich.

325
00:57:12.634 --> 00:57:15.719
In fact. I want all the
members of Operation Kino

326
00:57:15.803 --> 00:57:18.764
to receive the
Congressional Medal of Honor.

327
00:57:19.140 --> 00:57:22.851
Full citizenship for myself.
Well. that goes without saying.

328
00:57:23.144 --> 00:57:26.355
And I would like
the United States of America

329
00:57:26.439 --> 00:57:30.526
to purchase property for me
on Nantucket Island

330
00:57:30.610 --> 00:57:33.862
as a reward for all the
countless lives I've saved

331
00:57:33.947 --> 00:57:36.281
by bringing the tyranny of
the National Socialist Party

332
00:57:36.366 --> 00:57:39.993
to a swifter-than-imagined end.
Do you have all that. sir?

333
00:57:41.788 --> 00:57:45.249
I look forward to seeing you
face to face as well. sir.

334
00:57:46.125 --> 00:57:48.335
Lieutenant Raine?
Right here.

335
00:57:51.548 --> 00:57:52.756
Yes. sir.

336
00:57:52.840 --> 00:57:56.593
Colonel Landa will put you and
Private Utivich in a truck as prisoners.

337
00:57:56.678 --> 00:58:01.056
Then he and his radio operator will
get in the truck and drive to our lines.

338
00:58:01.140 --> 00:58:05.727
Upon crossing our lines. Colonel Landa
and his man will surrender to you.

339
00:58:05.812 --> 00:58:08.355
You will then take over
driving of the truck

340
00:58:08.439 --> 00:58:11.817
and bring them straight to me for
debriefing. Is that clear. Lieutenant?

341
00:58:11.901 --> 00:58:13.026
Yes. sir.

342
00:58:13.111 --> 00:58:14.570
Over and out.

343
01:03:58.748 --> 01:04:01.333
When I kill that guy. you got
30 feet to get to that guard.

344
01:04:01.417 --> 01:04:03.376
Can you do it?
I have to.

345
01:04:33.616 --> 01:04:34.950
Champagne?

346
01:05:26.794 --> 01:05:29.504
Who wants to send
a message to Germany?

347
01:05:30.339 --> 01:05:32.674
I have a message
for Germany.

348
01:05:36.137 --> 01:05:38.388
That you are
all going to die.

349
01:05:42.143 --> 01:05:47.564
And I want you to look deep into the
face of the Jew who's going to do it!

350
01:05:49.650 --> 01:05:52.736
Marcel. burn it down.

351
01:05:53.738 --> 01:05:55.238
Oui. Shosanna.

352
01:06:30.691 --> 01:06:32.817
My name
is Shosanna Dreyfus.

353
01:06:33.194 --> 01:06:34.778
and this is the face

354
01:06:36.739 --> 01:06:39.074
of Jewish vengeance.

355
01:08:44.742 --> 01:08:46.534
Hermann.
uncuff them.

356
01:09:05.179 --> 01:09:09.182
I'm officially surrendering myself
over to you. Lieutenant Raine.

357
01:09:10.309 --> 01:09:12.101
We're your prisoners.

358
01:09:12.937 --> 01:09:14.646
How about my knife?

359
01:09:20.611 --> 01:09:22.570
Thank you very much.
Colonel.

360
01:09:22.655 --> 01:09:25.740
Utivich. cuff the Colonel's
hands behind his back.

361
01:09:25.824 --> 01:09:28.034
Is that really
necessary?

362
01:09:28.118 --> 01:09:30.203
I'm a slave
to appearances.

363
01:09:33.374 --> 01:09:34.874
Scalp Hermann.

364
01:09:36.543 --> 01:09:38.211
Are you mad?

365
01:09:38.587 --> 01:09:40.338
What have you done?

366
01:09:40.839 --> 01:09:44.175
I made a deal with your
general for that man's life!

367
01:09:45.261 --> 01:09:48.638
Yeah. they made that deal. But they don't
give a fuck about him. They need you.

368
01:09:48.722 --> 01:09:50.682
You'll be shot for this!

369
01:09:51.350 --> 01:09:54.852
Nah. I don't think so. More like
chewed out. I've been chewed out before.

370
01:09:56.188 --> 01:10:00.358
You know. Utivich and myself heard
that deal you made with the brass.

371
01:10:00.818 --> 01:10:02.568
End the war tonight?

372
01:10:03.988 --> 01:10:05.530
I'd make that deal.

373
01:10:05.614 --> 01:10:07.448
How about you. Utivich?
You make that deal?

374
01:10:07.533 --> 01:10:08.533
I'd make that deal.

375
01:10:08.617 --> 01:10:11.119
I don't blame you.
Damn good deal.

376
01:10:11.870 --> 01:10:14.998
And that pretty little nest
you feathered for yourself.

377
01:10:15.082 --> 01:10:18.459
Well. if you're willing to
barbecue the whole High Command.

378
01:10:18.544 --> 01:10:21.546
I suppose that's worth
certain considerations.

379
01:10:22.298 --> 01:10:24.382
But I do have
one question.

380
01:10:25.467 --> 01:10:28.219
When you get to your little
place on Nantucket Island.

381
01:10:28.304 --> 01:10:32.849
I imagine you are going to take off that
handsome-looking SS uniform of yours.

382
01:10:32.933 --> 01:10:34.267
Ain't you?

383
01:10:38.230 --> 01:10:40.106
That's what I thought.

384
01:10:40.858 --> 01:10:42.734
Now. that I can't abide.

385
01:10:44.153 --> 01:10:46.446
How about you. Utivich.
can you abide it?

386
01:10:46.530 --> 01:10:48.406
Not one damn bit. sir.

387
01:10:50.034 --> 01:10:52.118
I mean.
if I had my way.

388
01:10:52.619 --> 01:10:57.081
you'd wear that goddamn uniform for
the rest of your pecker-sucking life.

389
01:10:58.584 --> 01:10:59.584
But I'm aware
that ain't practical.

390
01:10:59.668 --> 01:11:02.712
I mean. at some point.
you're going to have to take it off.

391
01:11:02.796 --> 01:11:03.921
So.

392
01:11:04.882 --> 01:11:08.593
I'm going to give you a little
something you can't take off.

393
01:11:33.535 --> 01:11:35.661
You know something.
Utivich?

394
01:11:36.038 --> 01:11:38.831
I think this just might be
my masterpiece.

395
